{# The controls that narrow a list, and nothing else. It fills `canvas.filters`
   (D8/D15): the two-column relation between the controls and the results is the
   canvas's, so this component owns no layout, no results region and no summary.
   The human asked for Linear's model — narrowing is done in an aside and what
   has been chosen is stated separately, above the rows — rather than for one row
   of pills doing both jobs at once (C22).

   NOTHING HERE SAYS "FACET". The aside is where a list is narrowed; whether that
   narrowing is a facet, an exposed filter or a saved view is a wiring question
   this ticket deliberately leaves open, and the vocabulary should not pre-empt
   it (D8).

   THE PANEL COLLAPSES BY COMPOSING `bb_theme:collapsible` rather than by
   carrying a second collapse of its own. That component is a native
   <details>/<summary> for a measured reason this panel shares exactly: Storybook
   never calls Drupal.attachBehaviors, so a scripted collapse would be a dead
   control on the surface the human reviews on — a click that answers with
   nothing is worse than no affordance at all. Composing it means there is ONE
   collapse mechanism in this theme, and the `Filters` heading IS the <summary>.
   The heading uses the existing body typography inside the summary.

   `collapsed` rather than `open`, because the panel's resting state is EXPANDED:
   a filter panel nobody can see is not a filter panel. The prop names the
   deviation from that resting state, the way `sidebar`'s does. It is passed
   through as `open: not collapsed`, so an absent prop leaves the panel open.
   What it no longer does is give the region its width back: the 192px track
   belongs to `canvas` now, which is the price of the aside not owning a layout.

   The heading is what the collapse is operated by, so a caller that omits
   `title` gets a chevron-only toggle.

   Spacing is the token scale (D16). Nothing here fetches, posts or persists a
   view.

   `layout: bar` IS THE SEARCH TOOLBAR above the rows (BB-592): not an aside,
   no heading and no collapse, the same surface as the panel, and its controls in
   ONE row — the first (the search) grows and wraps onto its own line before it
   would overflow, the later ones (the sort) keep their own width capped at the
   row. The row is 36px at compact density: its controls take the control-size
   token instead of a form's own height, inside an `inline-xs` inset and no
   border, and their labels stay only for screen readers. Its fields live
   OUTSIDE the exposed <form> (bound by the HTML `form` attribute), so BEF's
   autosubmit, which watches only the form's own elements,
   never sees them; the bar submits their form itself: a select on `change`, a
   text field 500ms after the last keystroke, and never the same value twice, so
   an Enter (which already submits natively) is not followed by a second request.
   `panel` is the default and the aside it always was, now filled with `bg-app`
   so it reads as a surface on the `bg-surface` main area. #}
{% set filters_controls %}{% block controls %}{{ controls }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set filters_actions %}{% block actions %}{{ actions }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set filters_pinned %}{% block pinned %}{{ pinned }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set has_pinned = filters_pinned|trim is not empty %}
{% set opener_label = active_count|default(0) > 0 ? 'Filters'|t ~ ' · ' ~ active_count : 'Filters'|t %}
{#- The bar and the toolbar submit their own fields: a select on change, a
    text field 500ms after the last keystroke, never the same value twice.
    A field inside an open dialog never submits: in the phone sheet, ticks wait for "Show results".
    A form with its own htmx trigger (Insights) applies itself; submitting it here would reload the page. -#}
{% set send_attributes %}x-data="{ send(field) { if (field.form && !field.closest('dialog[open]') && !['hx-get', 'data-hx-get', 'hx-trigger', 'data-hx-trigger'].some((name) => field.form.hasAttribute(name)) && field.dataset.sent !== field.value) { field.dataset.sent = field.value; field.form.requestSubmit(); } } }" @change="['search', 'text'].includes($event.target.type) || send($event.target)" @input.debounce.500ms="['search', 'text'].includes($event.target.type) && send($event.target)" @keydown.enter="['search', 'text'].includes($event.target.type) && ($event.target.dataset.sent = $event.target.value)"{% endset %}
{#- Every phone sheet: a change while it is open marks it dirty, "Show results"
    marks it applied, and closing it any other way (Close, Escape, an outside
    tap) reloads the page, so unapplied ticks never wait in the form for the
    next search keystroke to submit them. Close is visible because Safari has
    no `closedby` and a phone has no Escape key. -#}
{% set sheet_state %}x-on:change="$el.open && ($el.dataset.dirty = '1')" x-on:close="$el.dataset.dirty && !$el.dataset.applied && location.reload(); delete $el.dataset.dirty; delete $el.dataset.applied"{% endset %}
{% set sheet_close %}
    <div class="lg:hidden flex justify-end">
      {{ include('bb_theme:button', {
        variant: 'ghost',
        type: 'button',
        label: 'Close'|t,
        icon_only: true,
        icon: include('bb_theme:icon', { name: 'x-circle', size: 'md' }, with_context = false),
        attributes: create_attribute({ class: ['min-h-touch', 'min-w-touch'], 'x-on:click': '$refs.sheet.close()' }),
      }, with_context = false) }}
    </div>
{% endset %}
{% set show_results = "$refs.sheet.dataset.applied = '1'; " %}
{% set opener_attr = opener_id ? { id: opener_id } : {} %}
{% if layout|default('panel') == 'bar' %}
{#- With `sheet_for` the bar is the phone row above a panel whose own opener is
    off: below `lg` it drops its surface and adds a "Filters · N" opener for
    that panel's dialog. The opener comes AFTER the controls in the DOM so the
    `*:first` rules still reach the search; order alone moves it to the front
    and the search onto its own row. From `lg` up the bar is unchanged. -#}
<div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass([
    'flex', 'flex-row', 'flex-wrap', 'items-center', 'gap-inline',
    '*:first:flex-1', '*:first:basis-40', '*:first:min-w-0', '*:not-first:shrink-0', '*:not-first:max-w-full',
    '[&_label]:sr-only', '[&_input]:h-control', '[&_select]:h-control',
  ]|merge(sheet_for ? ['lg:p-inline-xs', 'lg:bg-app', 'lg:rounded-sm', 'max-lg:*:first:order-last', 'max-lg:*:first:basis-full'] : ['p-inline-xs', 'bg-app', 'rounded-sm'])) }} role="search"
  {%- if label %} aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %}
  {{ send_attributes }}>
  {{- filters_controls -}}
  {%- if sheet_for %}
  {{ include('bb_theme:button', {
    variant: 'neutral',
    type: 'button',
    label: opener_label,
    attributes: create_attribute({ class: ['min-h-touch', 'lg:hidden', 'max-lg:order-first'], 'data-sheet': sheet_for, 'x-on:click': 'document.getElementById($el.dataset.sheet)?.showModal()' }|merge(opener_attr)),
  }, with_context = false) }}
  {%- endif %}
</div>
{% elseif layout == 'toolbar' %}
{#- The board filter bar: no surface, one centred row of at least 36 px that
    wraps only when narrow. The controls group leads with the search (240 px);
    `actions` is a second group the row pushes to the right end
    (justify-between, no outer margin). `pinned` (the search) takes those
    240 px ahead of the controls, which then fill the row; with
    `pinned_width: auto` it keeps its natural width (Insights' period control).
    With `sheet`, below `lg` the row keeps only `pinned` and a "Filters · N"
    opener; `controls` and `actions` sit in a native <dialog> sheet, the
    panel's, which is `display: contents` from `lg` up, so one DOM serves both
    and the fields exist once. "Show results" submits the enclosing form. -#}
{% set controls_classes = ['flex', 'flex-wrap', 'items-center', 'gap-inline', 'min-w-0']
  |merge(has_pinned ? [sheet ? 'lg:flex-1' : 'flex-1'] : ['*:first:w-60', '*:first:shrink-0'])
  |merge(sheet ? ['max-lg:flex-col', 'max-lg:items-stretch'] : []) %}
{% set actions_classes = ['flex', 'flex-wrap', 'items-center', 'gap-inline']|merge(sheet ? ['max-lg:pt-stack'] : []) %}
<div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass([
    'flex', 'flex-row', 'flex-wrap', 'items-center', 'justify-between', 'gap-inline', 'min-h-9', 'min-w-0',
  ]) }} role="search"
  {%- if label %} aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %}
  {{ send_attributes }}>
  {%- if has_pinned %}
  {%- set pinned_search = pinned_width|default('search') == 'search' %}
  <div class="flex min-w-0 {{ sheet ? 'flex-1 lg:flex-none' ~ (pinned_search ? ' lg:w-60' : '') : (pinned_search ? 'w-60 shrink-0' : 'shrink-0') }}">{{ filters_pinned }}</div>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if sheet %}
  {{ include('bb_theme:button', {
    variant: 'neutral',
    type: 'button',
    label: opener_label,
    attributes: create_attribute({ class: ['min-h-touch', 'lg:hidden'], 'x-on:click': '$refs.sheet.showModal()' }|merge(opener_attr)),
  }, with_context = false) }}
  <dialog x-ref="sheet" aria-label="{{ 'Filters'|t }}" closedby="any" {{ sheet_state }} class="max-lg:w-full max-lg:max-w-full max-lg:max-h-5/6 max-lg:top-auto max-lg:p-stack max-lg:bg-app max-lg:text-text max-lg:border-0 max-lg:rounded-t-sm max-lg:overflow-y-auto lg:contents lg:text-inherit">
  {{- sheet_close }}
  {%- endif %}
  <div class="{{ controls_classes|join(' ') }}">{{ filters_controls }}</div>
  {%- if filters_actions|striptags|trim is not empty %}
  <div class="{{ actions_classes|join(' ') }}">{{ filters_actions }}</div>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if sheet %}
    <div class="lg:hidden pt-stack">
      {{ include('bb_theme:button', {
        variant: 'primary',
        type: 'button',
        label: 'Show results'|t,
        attributes: create_attribute({ class: ['w-full', 'min-h-touch'], 'x-on:click': show_results ~ "($el.closest('form') ?? $refs.sheet.querySelector('form'))?.requestSubmit(); $refs.sheet.close()" }),
      }, with_context = false) }}
    </div>
  </dialog>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
{% else %}
{#- Below `lg` the panel is a bottom sheet behind an opener; from `lg` up the
    aside is what it always was. ONE DOM: the aside is `display: contents` below
    `lg` and the dialog is `display: contents` from `lg` up, so the exposed
    form's fields exist once and never submit twice.
    The sheet is a native <dialog> opened with showModal(): the browser gives it
    the top layer, Escape, focus handling and `closedby`, it needs no Drupal
    behaviour, and it works the same in Storybook. With `opener: false` the
    panel shows nothing below `lg` until a bar opens its dialog by `sheet_id`. -#}
<aside{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass([
    'max-lg:contents', 'p-stack', 'bg-app', 'border', 'border-border-2', 'rounded-sm',
  ]) }}
  {%- if label %} aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %} x-data>
  {%- if opener is not same as(false) %}
  {{ include('bb_theme:button', {
    variant: 'neutral',
    type: 'button',
    label: active_count|default(0) > 0 ? title ~ ' · ' ~ active_count : title,
    attributes: create_attribute({ class: ['min-h-touch', 'lg:hidden'], 'x-on:click': '$refs.sheet.showModal()' }|merge(opener_attr)),
  }, with_context = false) }}
  {%- endif %}
  <dialog x-ref="sheet"{% if sheet_id %} id="{{ sheet_id }}"{% endif %} aria-label="{{ title }}" closedby="any"{% if sheet_open %} open{% endif %} {{ sheet_state }} class="max-lg:w-full max-lg:max-w-full max-lg:max-h-5/6 max-lg:top-auto max-lg:p-stack max-lg:bg-app max-lg:text-text max-lg:border-0 max-lg:rounded-t-sm max-lg:overflow-y-auto lg:contents lg:text-inherit">
    {{- sheet_close }}
    {% embed 'bb_theme:collapsible' with {
      open: not collapsed,
      attributes: create_attribute(),
    } %}
      {% block label %}<span class="text-body-strong text-title">{{ title }}</span>{% endblock %}
      {% block content %}
        <div class="flex flex-col items-stretch gap-group">{{ filters_controls }}</div>
      {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}
    <div class="lg:hidden pt-stack">
      {{ include('bb_theme:button', {
        variant: 'primary',
        type: 'button',
        label: 'Show results'|t,
        attributes: create_attribute({ class: ['w-full', 'min-h-touch'], 'x-on:click': show_results ~ "$refs.sheet.querySelector('form')?.requestSubmit(); $refs.sheet.close()" }),
      }, with_context = false) }}
    </div>
  </dialog>
</aside>
{% endif %}
